# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# The Silk Road: names and stories, by node (zh, en). Chapter nodes n1-n8 and the boss b; n0 the route's start.
SILK = {
 'name': ('丝绸之路', 'The Silk Road'),
 'start': ('玉门关外', 'Beyond the Jade Gate',
  '关门在身后合上时，守卒往地上泼了一碗酒，说是敬路上的人。你问敬哪些人，他不答，只把灯笼挑高了些。灯笼纸上有一行褪了色的墨字：「千里号，丁未年七月出关，计驼三百」。十年前出关的那支商队，没有一个人回来。如今朝廷重开商路，第一支出关的，是你们。',
  'When the gate shut behind you, a sentry poured a bowl of wine on the ground: for those on the road, he said. Which ones, you asked; he did not answer, only lifted his lantern higher. On its paper, in ink long faded: "The Thousand Li, out through the pass in the seventh month, three hundred camels." Not one of that caravan came back, ten years ago. Now the court opens the road again, and the first to go out are you.'),
 1: {
  'title': ('出关', 'Out of the Pass'),
  'n1': ('断旗墩', 'Broken-Banner Beacon', 'enemy',
   '烽燧上插着一面断旗，旗角已经被风撕成了絮。墩下的马贼不着急动手，像是在等谁先开口。他们的首领打了个唿哨，满坡的人一齐把刀拍在马鞍上，声音整齐得不像人。',
   'A broken banner stands on the beacon tower, its corners torn to threads by the wind. The bandits below are in no hurry; they seem to wait for someone to speak first. Their leader whistles, and every rider on the slope slaps his blade on his saddle at once, too evenly for men.'),
  'n2': ('白骨驿', 'White-Bone Post', 'story',
   '驿站里只住着一个老驿丞。他每晚点十二盏灯，第二天清早，总有一盏是灭的，灯油一滴不少。「少的那盏，是给借宿的人留的。」他说着，把你们的名字一笔一划记进簿子里。你瞥见上一页最后一个名字，墨迹还是湿的：千里号·账房。',
   'Only an old postmaster lives at the post. He lights twelve lamps every night; every morning one is out, its oil untouched. "That one is for the guest," he says, writing your names into his book stroke by stroke. On the page before, the last name is still wet: Thousand Li, the bookkeeper.'),
  'n3': ('风蚀谷', 'Wind-Carved Gorge', 'enemy2',
   '谷里的风会学人说话。先是驼铃，再是有人喊「停一停，等等我们」。沙匪就埋伏在风声里，等你们回头的那一瞬间扑上来。',
   'The wind in the gorge learns to talk. Camel bells first, then someone calling, "Wait for us, wait." The sand robbers lie in the sound of it, and rush you the moment you turn your heads.'),
  'n4': ('苦水井', 'Bitter Well', 'supply',
   '方圆百里只有这一口井，被一伙恶霸用铁链锁着，一桶水换一匹绢。打开井盖，水面上浮着一层细细的金粉。',
   'For a hundred li this is the only well, and a gang keeps it chained: a bucket of water for a bolt of silk. When the lid comes off, a film of fine gold dust floats on the water.'),
  'n5': ('互市旧址', 'Old Border Market', 'key',
   '残墙上还钉着当年的价牌：「石一车，易木一车半」。你们清出几间土屋，挂起朝廷的旗。第二天清早，墙外就有胡商牵着骆驼来叩门，像是一直在等。',
   'Price boards still hang on the ruined walls: "A cart of stone for a cart and a half of timber." You clear out a few mud rooms and raise the court\'s banner. Next morning foreign traders lead their camels up and knock, as if they had been waiting all along.'),
  'n6': ('胡商帐', 'The Sogdian\'s Tent', 'merchant',
   '帐里熏着说不出名字的香。胡商的眼睛是灰的，他说他在这片沙里做了三十年买卖，什么都卖，只是不收铜钱。',
   'Some nameless incense burns in the tent. The trader\'s eyes are grey; he says he has bought and sold in these sands for thirty years, anything at all, only never for copper.'),
  'n7': ('沙狐岭', 'Sand-Fox Ridge', 'enemy',
   '岭上的人披着狐皮，夜里眼睛会反光。他们不劫货，只劫人。领头的说：「把账本交出来，就放你们过去。」可你们身上没有账本。',
   'The men on the ridge wear fox skins, and their eyes catch the light at night. They take no goods, only people. "Give us the ledger and you may pass," says their leader. But you carry no ledger.'),
  'n8': ('无字碑', 'The Blank Stele', 'story',
   '路边立着一块没有字的碑。拿火把一照，碑面上浮出一行一行的小字，全是人名，后面跟着货物：「某某，绢二十，茶四十」。最后一行刚刚浮出来，写的是开拓队里一个兵的名字。',
   'A stele with no inscription stands by the road. In the torchlight, line after line of small characters rises on its face: names, each with goods. "So-and-so, silk twenty, tea forty." The last line is only now appearing. It is the name of one of your own men.'),
  'b': ('阳关故垒', 'Old Fort of Yang Pass', 'boss',
   '故垒的城头上站着一个独眼的马贼头子，人称「鹞子」。他不让路，也不谈价。「十年前我在这里放过一支商队，」他说，「后来每天夜里，都有骆驼来我帐外跪着。」他身后两翼的骑兵已经摆开了阵势。',
   'On the walls of the old fort stands a one-eyed bandit chief they call the Hawk. He will not stand aside, nor bargain. "Ten years ago I let a caravan through here," he says. "Since then, every night, camels come and kneel outside my tent." Behind him, horsemen spread out on both wings.'),
 },
 2: {
  'title': ('沙海', 'The Sea of Sand'),
  'n1': ('流沙口', 'Mouth of the Quicksand', 'enemy',
   '流沙会吞人，也会吐人。吐出来的人都穿着十年前的衣裳，眼神空空的，拦在路上不让你们走。',
   'The quicksand swallows people, and spits them out again. Those it gives back wear the clothes of ten years ago; their eyes are empty, and they stand across the road and will not let you pass.'),
  'n2': ('驼铃声', 'Bells with No Camels', 'story',
   '整整一夜，营地外都有驼铃响，一圈一圈地绕。天亮时沙地上满是蹄印，围着营地踩了三百圈，一圈不多，一圈不少。',
   'All night camel bells ring outside the camp, circling and circling. At dawn the sand is full of hoofprints, three hundred rings around the camp, not one more, not one fewer.'),
  'n3': ('黑沙暴', 'The Black Storm', 'enemy2',
   '天一下子黑了。沙暴里有人举着刀冲出来，砍完一刀又缩回风里。等风停了，地上一具尸体都没有。',
   'The sky goes black all at once. Men with blades burst out of the storm, strike once and shrink back into the wind. When it dies down there is not one body on the ground.'),
  'n4': ('月牙泉', 'Crescent Spring', 'supply',
   '一弯泉水卧在沙山之间，千年不涸。占泉的马帮头领说，泉水是给死人照镜子的。你们低头一看，水里映出的队伍比岸上多出好几十人。',
   'A crescent of water lies between the dunes, dry in no thousand years. The caravan boss who holds it says the spring is a mirror for the dead. You look down: the column in the water is dozens longer than the one on the bank.'),
  'n5': ('鬼市', 'The Ghost Market', 'key',
   '只有月圆的夜里，沙海深处才会亮起一条街。摊主们不抬头，不说话，只伸出手比价。你们拿木头换了粮，拿来的粮是新的，装粮的麻袋上却印着「千里号」。从此每晚，鬼市都给开拓队留一个摊位。',
   'Only on nights of the full moon does a street light up deep in the sea of sand. The stall-keepers never look up, never speak, only hold out their hands to name a price. You trade timber for grain; the grain is new, but the sacks are stamped "Thousand Li." From then on, every night, the ghost market keeps a stall for you.'),
  'n6': ('驼队营地', 'Caravanserai', 'merchant',
   '一支大驼队在这里歇脚，帐篷连成了一座小城。领队是个女人，说话带着东边的口音。她卖的东西都很好，就是价钱从来不肯少。',
   'A great caravan rests here, its tents a small town. Its leader is a woman with an eastern accent. Everything she sells is good, and she never lowers a price.'),
  'n7': ('白龙堆', 'White Dragon Mounds', 'enemy',
   '土台一座连着一座，像一条睡着的白龙。马贼把这里当作迷宫，绕着土台放冷箭。',
   'Earthen mounds stand one after another like a sleeping white dragon. The bandits use them as a maze, shooting from behind them as you wind through.'),
  'n8': ('沙中城', 'The Buried City', 'story',
   '风掀开沙丘，露出半座城。城门上的匾额写着「千里」二字。城里的市集摆得整整齐齐，货架上落满了沙，账台上压着一封没封口的信：「货已到，人未归」。',
   'The wind peels back a dune and half a city appears. The board over its gate reads "Thousand Li." Inside, the market stands in perfect order, sand thick on every shelf; on the counting desk, under a weight, an unsealed letter: "The goods arrived. The men did not."'),
  'b': ('马贼王帐', 'The Bandit King\'s Tent', 'boss',
   '沙海里所有的马贼都向这顶金帐纳贡。马贼王坐在一张驼骨椅上，椅背上刻着三百个名字。「他们欠我的路钱，」他说，「到今天还没还清。你们来替他们还？」',
   'Every bandit in the sea of sand pays tribute to this golden tent. The Bandit King sits on a throne of camel bone; three hundred names are carved on its back. "They owe me road money," he says, "and have not paid it yet. Have you come to pay for them?"'),
 },
 3: {
  'title': ('佛窟', 'The Thousand Buddha Caves'),
  'n1': ('崖下伏兵', 'Ambush under the Cliff', 'enemy',
   '崖壁上凿满了窟龛，每一龛里都坐着一尊佛。伏兵就藏在佛像后面，箭从佛的指缝里射出来。',
   'The cliff is honeycombed with niches, a Buddha seated in each. The ambush hides behind the statues; arrows fly from between the Buddhas\' fingers.'),
  'n2': ('变画', 'The Changing Mural', 'story',
   '第一百二十窟的壁画上画着一支商队。守窟的老僧说，这画每天都不一样：昨天驼队还在关内，今天已经过了沙海。你们细看，画里最后一峰骆驼背上，坐着一个和你一模一样的人。',
   'The mural in the hundred-and-twentieth cave shows a caravan. The old monk who keeps the caves says it is never the same two days running: yesterday the camels were still inside the pass, today they have crossed the sea of sand. Look closely: on the last camel sits someone exactly like you.'),
  'n3': ('窟前僧兵', 'Warrior Monks at the Caves', 'enemy2',
   '僧兵们拿着铁棍守在窟前，说开拓队身上带着「不干净的东西」，不许进山。问他们是什么东西，他们齐声念了一句经，就冲了上来。',
   'Warrior monks with iron staves guard the caves; they say you carry "something unclean" and may not enter the mountain. Ask them what, and they chant a line of scripture as one and charge.'),
  'n4': ('寺前粥棚', 'The Gruel Shed', 'supply',
   '寺门前搭着施粥的棚子，被一伙假和尚霸占，一碗粥要一两银子。赶走他们以后，真正的僧人回来了，说这棚子十年前就是为一支商队搭的，粥一直熬着，没人来喝。',
   'Before the temple gate stands a shed for giving out gruel, seized by false monks who charge a tael a bowl. When they are gone the real monks return; the shed, they say, was put up ten years ago for a caravan, and the gruel has been kept on the boil ever since. No one came to eat it.'),
  'n5': ('藏经洞', 'The Sealed Library', 'key',
   '洞里堆满了经卷，还有一摞一摞的账册，记着这一路上所有的买卖。你们从账册里抄出几条老商路的价钱，派人去问，竟都还作数。',
   'The cave is piled with sutras, and with ledger after ledger recording every trade along this road. You copy out the prices of a few old routes and send to ask: every one of them still holds.'),
  'n6': ('画匠铺', 'The Painters\' Shop', 'merchant',
   '画匠们给石窟描金上彩，也替人画像。他们说，画得像的，人就能多活十年。他们也卖别的东西，从不问来路。',
   'The painters gild and colour the caves, and paint portraits too: a good likeness, they say, adds ten years to a life. They sell other things besides, and never ask where they came from.'),
  'n7': ('断崖栈', 'The Broken Gallery', 'enemy',
   '连接上下窟的栈道断了一截。对面的人站在断口上看着你们，手里拿着当年千里号的令牌。',
   'A stretch of the gallery between the upper and lower caves has fallen away. Men stand at the far edge watching you, holding the Thousand Li\'s tallies of ten years ago.'),
  'n8': ('无面佛', 'The Faceless Buddha', 'story',
   '最深的一窟里坐着一尊没有脸的大佛。佛前供着三百盏灯，灭了一大半。老僧说：灯灭一盏，就有一个千里号的人「到了」。到了哪里，他也不知道。',
   'In the deepest cave sits a great Buddha with no face. Before it burn three hundred lamps; more than half have gone out. Each lamp that goes out, the old monk says, is one of the Thousand Li who has "arrived." Arrived where, he does not know.'),
  'b': ('千佛洞主', 'Master of the Thousand Buddhas', 'boss',
   '洞主戴着一张金色的面具，自称守着这座山已经十年。「你们要找的人，」他说，「都在这面墙上。」墙上画着三百个商人，每个人的脸都被刮掉了。他抬手，身后的金面卫一齐拔刀。',
   'The Master wears a golden mask and says he has kept this mountain for ten years. "Those you seek," he says, "are all on this wall." Three hundred merchants are painted there, every face scraped away. He lifts a hand; the gold-masked guards behind him draw as one.'),
 },
 4: {
  'title': ('绿洲王城', 'The Oasis Kingdom'),
  'n1': ('城外戍堡', 'Outer Fort', 'enemy',
   '王城外的戍堡里驻着一队兵，穿的是关内的旧式甲胄。他们奉命不许任何商队进城，十年来一直如此。',
   'A troop holds the fort outside the royal city, in armour of an old style from inside the pass. Their orders are to let no caravan in; for ten years they have kept them.'),
  'n2': ('账房先生', 'The Bookkeeper\'s Letters', 'story',
   '城里人人都知道一个「账房先生」，说他算账从不出错，十年前来到这里，帮国王管了国库。你们在客栈收到他的一封信，信里只写了一句话：「白骨驿那盏灯，是我点的。」',
   'Everyone in the city knows of "the bookkeeper": his sums are never wrong; he came ten years ago and has kept the king\'s treasury ever since. At the inn a letter from him awaits you. It holds one line: "The lamp at White-Bone Post: I lit it."'),
  'n3': ('葡萄园伏兵', 'Ambush in the Vineyards', 'enemy2',
   '葡萄架连成一片绿海，伏兵就藏在藤下。他们的刀上都刻着同一个记号：一峰骆驼，背上驮着一盏灯。',
   'The vine trellises make a green sea, and the ambush hides beneath. Every blade bears the same mark: a camel carrying a lamp on its back.'),
  'n4': ('王城驿馆', 'The Royal Hostel', 'supply',
   '驿馆被国舅的家丁占着，专门敲诈外来的商人。把他们赶出去以后，馆里的老仆给你们备了酒饭，说这都是十年前就备下的。',
   'The queen\'s brother\'s men hold the hostel, to squeeze foreign merchants. When they are thrown out, an old servant sets wine and food before you, and says it was all laid by ten years ago.'),
  'n5': ('万国商馆', 'Hall of Ten Thousand Nations', 'key',
   '商馆里挂着各国的旗，独缺一面。你们把朝廷的旗挂上去的时候，满堂的商人都站了起来。从这天起，西域的货能直接运回关内了。',
   'The hall hangs the banners of every nation but one. When you raise the court\'s banner in its place, every merchant in the hall rises to his feet. From this day the goods of the west can go straight back through the pass.'),
  'n6': ('王城西市', 'The West Market', 'merchant',
   '西市里什么都有，连长生的药都有人卖。一个白胡子老人守着一只小葫芦，说这里面的丹药能让人「从头再来」，一天只卖一颗。',
   'The West Market has everything; someone even sells medicine for long life. An old man with a white beard keeps a small gourd: the pills in it, he says, let a man "begin again." He sells one a day.'),
  'n7': ('金面卫营', 'Camp of the Golden Masks', 'enemy',
   '金面卫是国王的亲军，戴着和千佛洞主一样的面具。他们不说话，不吃饭，夜里也不睡觉，只是一遍一遍地操练。',
   'The Golden Masks are the king\'s own guard, in the same masks as the Master of the Thousand Buddhas. They do not speak, nor eat, nor sleep at night; they only drill, over and over.'),
  'n8': ('王宫夜宴', 'Night Banquet at the Palace', 'story',
   '国王设宴款待开拓队。宴席上坐满了宾客，一个个都不动筷子。国王举杯：「敬千里号。」满堂宾客跟着举杯，你这才看清，他们袖口上都缝着同一个字：「千」。',
   'The king holds a banquet for you. The tables are full of guests, and not one of them touches his chopsticks. The king raises his cup: "To the Thousand Li." The hall raises its cups after him, and only then do you see: every guest has the same character sewn into his cuff. "Thousand."'),
  'b': ('绿洲王', 'King of the Oasis', 'boss',
   '王座上的人摘下了王冠，露出一张平凡的脸。「我就是那个账房，」他说，「十年前我把商队的账算错了一笔，从那天起，他们就停在了路上，一步也走不动。」他站起来，金面卫列阵护在两侧。「要过去，就先把这笔账算清。」',
   'The man on the throne lifts off his crown, and his face is an ordinary one. "I am the bookkeeper," he says. "Ten years ago I got one sum of the caravan\'s wrong, and from that day they have stood still on the road, unable to move a step." He rises; the Golden Masks form up on either side. "If you would pass, first settle that account."'),
 },
}
